  "user_request_original": "Design a 20-layer alternating Ta2O5/SiO2 bandpass filter on fused silica substrate with air incident medium. Layers 1-7 and 18-20 are optimization variables initialized at quarter-wave optical thickness for 1450 nm wavelength (Ta2O5 QWOT ≈ 1450/(4*n_H), SiO2 QWOT ≈ 1450/(4*n_L)) with ±10% random perturbation. Layers 8-17 are fixed constants at exactly 215.0 nm. Optimization bounds for free layers: [100, 400] nm. Apply L2 curvature penalty to objective function penalizing adjacent-layer thickness differences exceeding 30 nm. Evaluate coherent TMM across 1300-1800 nm. Score three weighted objectives: (1) transmittance at 1550 nm, (2) mean transmittance in 1400-1500 nm, (3) mean transmittance in 1600-1700 nm. Total layer count: exactly 20 layers. Canonical user controls: wavelength intervals 1400-1500 nm, 1550-1550 nm, 1600-1700 nm. soft objectives: high transmittance at 1550 nm (soft target ≥ 0.95); strong suppression of transmittance in 1400-1500 nm and 1600-1700 nm. behaviors to suppress or avoid: transmittance in 1400-1500 nm; transmittance in 1600-1700 nm. manufacturing constraints: total layers ≤ 30.",
  "normalized_request_english": "Coherently optimize 20 alternating Ta2O5/SiO2 layers on fused silica from 1300 to 1800 nm at normal incidence. Free layers 1-7 and 18-20 vary in [100, 400] nm. Layers 8-17 fixed at 215 nm. Maximize transmittance at 1550 nm while minimizing mean transmittance in 1400-1500 nm and 1600-1700 nm bands under ±10% manufacturing tolerance.",
